1
00:00:00,535 --> 00:00:01,705
(Leonard:)Great.

2
00:00:01,869 --> 00:00:04,499
(Sheldon:)So I've decided
I'm going to collaborate with you.

3
00:00:07,667 --> 00:00:09,207
(Leonard:)Great.

4
00:00:09,377 --> 00:00:11,207
So, what exactly is it you do?

5
00:00:12,255 --> 00:00:16,295
(Sheldon:)I know you chatter on about it all the time,
but I've never really paid attention.

6
00:00:17,009 --> 00:00:20,219
(Leonard:)Right now, I'm designing an experiment
to study the soft component...

7
00:00:20,388 --> 00:00:23,138
...of cosmic radiation at sea level,
but I don't need help.

8
00:00:23,307 --> 00:00:25,347
(Sheldon:)Oh, sure you do.

9
00:00:25,810 --> 00:00:28,480
(Sheldon:)Now see, what's this here in the schematic,
a laser array?

10
00:00:28,646 --> 00:00:30,356
(Raj:)- Yes.
- Now, hmm...

11
00:00:33,693 --> 00:00:36,733
(Sheldon:)What happens if you use argon lasers
instead of helium-neon?

12
00:00:37,155 --> 00:00:39,235
- It would blow up.
- Are you sure?

13
00:00:39,740 --> 00:00:42,240
- Pretty sure.
- "Pretty sure" is not very scientific.

14
00:00:42,410 --> 00:00:46,200
Is this how you normally work?
Just hunches and guesses and stuff?

15
00:00:47,081 --> 00:00:48,211
(Leonard:)Okay.

16
00:00:48,374 --> 00:00:51,414
(Leonard:)I understand that you're going
through a bit of a career crisis.

17
00:00:51,586 --> 00:00:55,426
(Leonard:)You're searching for some other area
where you can feel valuable and productive.

18
00:00:55,590 --> 00:00:58,130
(Leonard:)But I need to tell you something,
and listen carefully.

